# Milestone: M3
# Covers: errors in detached code are displayed; parent block is stopped on
#         error in sequential code; detach() call propagation semantics.
# defer-to: M4 (requires detach() builtin function and ',' / '&' separator runtime)
#
# Reason:
#   The fixture calls the detach() builtin function, which is a stdlib helper
#   scheduled for M4.  It also uses ',' and '&' separators which require the
#   urbi_step driver (M5 chk path).  Error propagation across concurrent
#   strands depends on the full scheduler context.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M4+ with detach() builtin):
# # f;
# # [00000001:error] !!! input.u:@.1: lookup failed: f
# # f,
# # [00000002:error] !!! input.u:@.1: lookup failed: f
# # detach(f)|;
# # ... (see legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/detach-error.chk)
